    {
      "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.44e5331cbf5f11d200a6fb3197185953b621a9b8.001.1",
      "event": "Flood Advisory",
      "severity": "Minor",
      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 29 at 1:21PM HST until October 29 at 4:15PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Windward Big Island.\n\n* WHEN...Until 415 PM HST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding on roads, poor drainage areas, and in\nstreams. Water over roadways.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 118 PM HST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain over Puna and\nSouth Hilo districts. Rain was falling at a rate of 1 to 2 inches\nper hour with the heaviest rain near Glenwood and Mountain View.\nMinor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly in the\nadvisory area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nHilo, Hawaiian Paradise Park, Mountain View, Glenwood, Keaau,\nHawaiian Acres, Orchidlands Estates, Volcano, Papaikou, Pahoa and\nPepeekeo.",
      "instruction": "Stay away from streams, drainage ditches and low lying areas prone to\nflooding.\n\nA Flood Watch is also in effect for Big Island until 6 PM HST.",
      "areaDesc": "Hawaii in Hawaii, HI",
      "zones": [],
      "effective": "2026-10-29T13:21:00-10:00",
