    {
      "id": "urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0437844be0ca8dcc561a28b9c8dfe6775a73cd4c.001.1",
      "event": "Flood Advisory",
      "severity": "Minor",
      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 29 at 12:24PM HST until October 29 at 1:45PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...West Maui in Maui County...\n\n* WHEN...Until 145 PM HST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding on roads, poor drainage areas, and in\nstreams.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1221 PM HST, Doppler radar indicated moderate to locally heavy\nrain over the windward areas of the West Maui. Rain was falling\nat a rate of 0.5 to 1 inch per hour with the heaviest rain over\nKahakuloa. Minor flooding is ongoing in the advisory area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nKahului, Kahakuloa, Waihee, Honokohau, Waiehu, Kapalua, Wailuku,\nNapili-Honokowai, Kaanapali, Waikapu and Honolua Bay.",
      "instruction": "Stay away from streams, drainage ditches and low lying areas prone to\nflooding.\n\nA Flood Watch is also in effect for Maui until 6pm HST.",
      "areaDesc": "Maui, HI",
